# Settings for the devcontainer:* tasks and the bootstrap scripts. Copy to
# .devcontainer/.env (gitignored) and uncomment what you need. Every value can
# also be set as a plain environment variable; explicit CLI parameters win.
# Loaded by Task (root Taskfile `dotenv:`) and by bootstrap.ps1/bootstrap.sh.
# Precedence in the tasks: a var on the command line
# (`task devcontainer:up DEVCONTAINER_DOCKER_PATH=docker`) beats this file,
# which beats an exported environment variable. Nothing in here is a
# credential; it holds machine-local choices only.

# Docker-compatible CLI handed to `devcontainer --docker-path`: a command name
# on PATH (docker, wslc, podman, nerdctl, finch) or a full path. Unset =
# docker on PATH, else wslc.exe on Windows. Images, containers and named
# volumes belong to the engine chosen: keep to one engine per machine.
#DEVCONTAINER_DOCKER_PATH=wslc

# Portable Node.js and @devcontainers/cli versions used by the host-side
# tasks (cached per user; nothing installed globally).
#DEVCONTAINER_NODE_VERSION=24.21.0
#DEVCONTAINER_CLI_VERSION=latest

# Root of the host-side folders that devcontainer.json bind-mounts for tool
# state (task devcontainer:homes). Default: %USERPROFILE%\.devcontainer-homes
# on Windows, ~/.devcontainer-homes elsewhere. The mounts in devcontainer.json
# name the folder literally, so change both or neither.
#DEVCONTAINER_HOMES=

# Command `task devcontainer:stop` runs inside the container before it stops
# it; a non-zero exit refuses the stop (FORCE=1 skips it). Unset = the repo's
# `task shutdown:check`, else the devhost Feature's devhost-shutdown-check, else
# none (bootstrap/SHUTDOWN.md). Set it only to override that.
#STOP_CHECK=

# The Claude Code host session: the UUID of the one session `task
# devcontainer:claude` resumes (created under that UUID if it does not exist
# yet). The name shown in Claude Code is only a label and may change with
# /rename; the UUID (see /status) finds the session. HOST_SESSION_<DIR> does
# the same for a sub-folder started with DIR=<path> (DIR=rooms/solis reads
# HOST_SESSION_SOLIS). Unset: a plain new session.
#HOST_SESSION=

# Bootstrap only: which ref of nabil-becker/devcontainer-features to vendor
# from, an alternative source (URL base or local checkout), and whether to
# stop before `task devcontainer:up`.
#DEVCONTAINER_BOOTSTRAP_REF=main
#DEVCONTAINER_BOOTSTRAP_SOURCE=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nabil-becker/devcontainer-features/main
#DEVCONTAINER_BOOTSTRAP_NO_UP=true
